{
  "inShort": "The team is at risk: no playable slice or test results were shown. The devlog reports five testers, but no build or playtest document was added. What game work got done remains unknown; the landscape image and film reference do not demonstrate the goal.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x0600jscsz8r4935jty",
      "text": "The public repository of Godot demo projects is done. Its folders, MIT license and import instructions match the task, but do not demonstrate this game's sailing or tides."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x0s00jtcsz8az0lkwpy",
      "text": "The animated reference video for the art style remains done. The title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny. The video was not watched, so its suitability as an animated reference remains unverified."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x1800jucsz8wothj7j8",
      "text": "The reference article on what playtesting is is done. The Wikipedia article explains testing purposes and formats. It does not supply results from the five reported players."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x1q00jvcsz8qpwzz58f",
      "text": "The private design board for the team is marked done. No board contents were shown this sprint, so it adds no visible evidence about the slice."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "Where can the reported playtest document and the tested build be opened?",
    "What did the five players complete, what failed, and what did the team learn?",
    "Did the tested build include two islands, flooding and draining, and two-player sailing?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlog #3 told the audience five players tried the tide loop; it received 0 applause and 0 views, and the project lists no store page or playable link.",
    "team": "Only 10–15 hours a week are stated, so the known checkpoint budget is 40–60 hours. Alex confirmed all three weeks; Mia stopped confirming after week one, leaving engineering capacity for tides and co-op unconfirmed.",
    "management": "With seven of 28 days left, four tasks are done and the storyboard is cut, but none demonstrates the playable-slice goal. Publishing the prototype devlog meets the stage's sole required task, yet the shown evidence establishes neither a proven core nor a chosen style for the eventual release."
  }
}

